# Imports

- Always use static `import` statements. **NEVER** use dynamic `await import()`.
  All dependencies must be resolved at module load time. Dynamic imports cause
  Vite chunk warnings and make dependency graphs harder to trace.
- Exception: `?raw` imports are used for bundling markdown as strings
  (e.g. `import GUIDE from './guide.md?raw'`). These are handled by Vite at
  build time.
- **No convenience re-exports of types (or values).** Do not add
  `export type { Foo } from './other'` at the end of an unrelated module so
  callers can import `Foo` from the wrong file. Import from the **defining
  module** (e.g. `import type { Foo } from './types'`). Convenience re-exports
  are easy to leave stale when types move and they obscure the real source of
  truth.

See also **`absolute-imports.mdc`** for the `@/*` alias rules (cross-directory
imports must use `@/...`; same-directory imports use `./`).
